Serial ports without a platform Bluetooth.

The serial port manager enumerates Bluetooth serial ports alongside the
wired ones, creating the Bluetooth adapter without asking whether the
platform has one. A Linux build without BlueZ (use_bluez = false, zebkit's)
has only bluetooth_adapter_stub.cc, whose CreateAdapter() is NOTREACHED():
navigator.serial.requestPort() and getPorts() crashed the browser process.
Without platform Bluetooth, GetDevices() returns the wired ports and
OpenPort() of an unknown token fails, as they would with no Bluetooth ports.
docs/SYSTEM_INTEGRATION.md, section 10.

